% Brownfield unit: evidence-gated advanced techniques in generic mix building.
% Govern brain/advanced_mix.py and its plan_mix_build/revision integration.

<pdd-interface>
{"type":"module","module":{"functions":[{"name":"compile_generic","signature":"(plan: dict, recipe: dict) -> dict","returns":"dict"},{"name":"upgrade","signature":"(plan: dict, recipe_path: Path) -> dict","returns":"dict"}]}}
</pdd-interface>

% Vocabulary
<vocabulary>
invalid: a recipe failing a declared schema, numeric, approval, hash, source
region, phase, note, envelope or deck-allocation requirement.
</vocabulary>
An approved recipe is a version-one local advanced_mix.json in the named plan
directory, containing approved=true and measured evidence for every finalized
foreground recording. Evidence includes SHA-256, source BPM, source duration,
shared pattern zero, confidence >=0.9 and measured pitch residual within 15 cents.
The native clock uses one explicitly chosen tempo and a 4/8/16-beat pattern.
Recipe presence participates in plan input revisions; absence preserves legacy
revision behavior. Generic-generated performances carry generic-measured-v1
provenance. Human-authored performances retain the existing generic-Build guard.

% Requirements
Preserve the optimized track set/order, effective DJ notes, bunches, cue points,
ride counts, transition overrides and selected mix profile. Use the existing
native performance compiler and runner for source loops, independent copies,
deck allocation, drift monitoring and cleanup. The normal planner still runs
first. Unsupported conventional recipes decline the upgrade with an inspectable
reason. Source BPM correction is bounded to +/-8% at this stage. Explicit
opener effects, tempo/pitch holds, acapella layers and dramatic exits keep their
conventional execution. A measured cue may not be silently moved to fix phase.

Same-song forward handoffs must exactly match effective skip_handoff notes;
backward handoffs require allow_reentry. Use overlapping copies of the original
with a four-count handoff inside the chosen body, away from entry/exit blends.
Short intro extension requires allow_intro_extension and a confirmed first
verse boundary. Repeat only an approved pre-verse span, two or three plays,
and prove it covers the entire incoming gentle blend. Preserve backbeat/pattern
phase through every repeat and handoff. Do not loop a verse to hide a short intro.

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Compile an advanced plan only with approved measured evidence and matching original source hashes for every foreground recording.
R2 (MUST): Preserve finalized foreground identities and order and every effective mandatory source limit or excluded interval through repeats and handoffs.
R3 (MUST NOT): Move an approved cue or invent an alignment to repair an invalid measured pattern phase.
R4 (MUST): Use at least 24 counts for native eased different-song fader blends, keeping peak fader speed within the sixteen-count linear gentle rule.
R5 (MUST NOT): Render audio, replace original recordings, connect to Mixxx or start playback during compilation.
R6 (MUST): Return identical conventional events plus a decline reason when an optional recipe is invalid, unsupported, incomplete or stale.
R7 (MUST NOT): Replace an authored performance with generic Build; allow rebuilding only a performance marked as generated by this unit.
R8 (MUST): Validate the compiled timeline for source regions, phase and available decks before publishing it.
</contract_rules>

% Verification
Synthetic source files and the generic builder exercise valid native schedules,
hash/tempo/pitch/phase failures, mandatory boundaries, exclusion-safe forward
handoffs, backward permission, short-intro coverage/verse refusal, capped loop
plays, overlap/deck allocation, authored protection and revision participation.
Run tests.test_advanced_mix and the focused workflow regressions. A dry-run/fake
device proves scheduling and refusal behavior, not audible musical quality.
